  "kind": "graph",
  "id": "osf-builder-family-and-post-placement",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-11T14:13:45.632Z",
  "title": "Builder-family detection and diff-aware review posting",
  "summary": "This change makes two parts of the review pipeline stricter and more forgiving at once. Builder-family detection now reads every word of a `Code-Generator:` trailer's model name (vendor names and model ids alike), refuses to guess when words point at different families, and treats a commit with no trailer as making the whole range unknown — except a clean merge, which `git merge-tree --write-tree` proves introduces nothing of its own. An unknown builder family now fails the run closed: no reviewer counts, the outcome is could-not-run, and the reason quotes the offending trailer. On the posting side, the pull request's diff is fetched and parsed so findings outside it go into the review body instead of an inline comment GitHub would reject with HTTP 422; a diff GitHub refuses no longer stops the review, and an over-long body is cut and marked rather than refused.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
